# Water Data ToolBox App

This package provides a CLI-only packaged app for the Water Data ToolBox workflows. The GUI code remains in the repo, but the packaged executable does not route into it.

## Local package runs

From the repo root, use the `src/` layout directly:

```bash
PYTHONPATH=src python -m waterdata_toolbox_demo --help
PYTHONPATH=src python -m waterdata_toolbox_demo create-new-project --discharge
PYTHONPATH=src python -m waterdata_toolbox_demo add-data --discharge
```

If you prefer an installed package workflow:

```bash
pip install -e .
python -m waterdata_toolbox_demo --help
python -m waterdata_toolbox_demo create-new-project --discharge --daily
python -m waterdata_toolbox_demo add-data --periodic
```

## CLI examples

Create New Project:

```bash
PYTHONPATH=src python -m waterdata_toolbox_demo create-new-project \
  --bbox -82.859 31.899 -82.013 32.947 \
  --discharge \
  --daily \
  --output-dir outputs/usgs_waterdata_demo
```

Adding Data to Project:

```bash
PYTHONPATH=src python -m waterdata_toolbox_demo add-data \
  --periodic \
  --station-id 410947071344803 \
  --parameter-code 72019 \
  --start-date 1880-01-01 \
  --end-date 2100-01-01 \
  --output-dir outputs/usgs_waterdata_demo
```

## Outputs

- `add-data` writes one CSV artifact per run.
- Daily workflows keep the custom metadata preamble:
  - `# site_no,Description,Parameter,Statistic,TS_ID,IV_TS_ID`
  - `Time,Daily values,Approval status,Qualifier`
- `create-new-project` writes one shapefile set per selected workflow:
  - `discharge.shp`
  - `daily.shp`
  - `periodic.shp`
- The shapefile schema is intentionally reduced for readability and format safety. See `docs/create-new-project-shapefile-fields.md`.

## Windows app build

Build the packaged Windows app on Windows, not macOS. From a Windows environment with the project checked out:

```bash
pip install -e .[build]
pyinstaller waterdata_toolbox_demo.spec
```

The default build emits an `onedir` app for faster startup. Launch the packaged app from:

```text
dist/waterdata_toolbox_demo/waterdata_toolbox_demo.exe
```

Launching the packaged app with no arguments prints CLI help and exits.
